* pt_wtx_ext_rx: receiver for the WTX_EXT_P/N east debug pair (fallback route
* wire_tx_external_data).  Per spec/consolidation-pass.md item 6 this is one
* instance of the timing family's shared differential receiver
* pt_diff_clk_rx (analog/timing/diff_clk_rx.spice); no separate design.
*
*   WTX_EXT_P/N  pad side (after the pads family's protection)
*   EN           debug.wtx_ext.enable (the same control drives pt_wiredtx WTX_EXT)
*   DX           to pt_wiredtx DX (selected break-before-make in pt_wtx_predrv)
*   DXB          complement (unused by pt_wiredtx; available for observation)
*   PRESENT      receiver activity detector -> status (wtx_ext presence)
*   ATB_DET      detector node -> atb_tap
* SE is tied low: differential (qualified) mode.  Per timing's data-mode
* check, DX is taken from OUTN (OUTP has 2-3x the edge spread) with the
* pad legs swapped so the polarity is preserved.  Board/FPGA requirement
* B12: AC-coupled source sends >= 128 balanced bits (e.g. 1010) before
* payload.  EN=0 is the safe state; the pre-driver ignores DX unless
* WTX_EXT selects it.
.include ../timing/diff_clk_rx.spice

.subckt pt_wtx_ext_rx WTX_EXT_P WTX_EXT_N EN DX DXB PRESENT ATB_DET VDD VSS
XRX WTX_EXT_N WTX_EXT_P EN VSS DXB DX PRESENT ATB_DET VDD VSS pt_diff_clk_rx
.ends pt_wtx_ext_rx
